If a patient has a concurrent-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-use and has an unpredictable-medication-use then the concurrent-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-use can likely have a greater-than-stable-lower-dosage-use-risk.
If a patient has a concurrent-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-use and has a higher-dosage-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-combination then the concurrent-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-use can likely have a greater-than-stable-lower-dosage-use-risk.
If a patient has a concurrent-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-use and has an other-substance-use then the concurrent-opioid-and-benzodiazepine-use can likely have a greater-than-stable-lower-dosage-use-risk.
An other-substance-example is an alcohol-example.
